</style>
</head>
<body>

<!-- ============ HEADER ============ -->
<header class="report-header">
  <div class="container">
    <h1>BIEK Computer Science Past Paper Analysis</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">A comprehensive trend analysis of question types, volume patterns, and topic distribution across 11 years (2015–2025) of HSC Part-2 examinations under the Board of Intermediate Education Karachi.</p>
    <p class="meta">Report prepared for educators &amp; curriculum planners &nbsp;·&nbsp; Data source: 327 questions from BIEK official past papers &nbsp;·&nbsp; April 2026</p>
  </div>
</header>

<div class="container">

<!-- ============================== SECTION 1 ============================== -->
<section class="section" id="overview">
  <h2 class="section-title"><span class="section-number">1</span>Dataset &amp; Examination Overview</h2>

  <div class="kpi-grid">
    <div class="kpi-card accent">
      <div class="kpi-value">327</div>
      <div class="kpi-label">Total Questions</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card purple">
      <div class="kpi-value">10</div>
      <div class="kpi-label">Active Exam Years</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card mcq">
      <div class="kpi-value">150</div>
      <div class="kpi-label">MCQs (45.9%)</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card short">
      <div class="kpi-value">147</div>
      <div class="kpi-label">Short Questions (44.9%)</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card long">
      <div class="kpi-value">30</div>
      <div class="kpi-label">Long Questions (9.2%)</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card red">
      <div class="kpi-value">2020</div>
      <div class="kpi-label">Missing Year (COVID-19)</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>Scope &amp; Methodology</h3>
    <p>This analysis is based on a community-compiled dataset of <strong>327 examination questions</strong> from BIEK Computer Science Paper-II (theory portion), covering the years <strong>2015 through 2025</strong>. Each question is classified by year, type (MCQs, Short, or Long), and full question text. The year <strong>2020 is absent</strong> from the dataset — consistent with the examination cancellations during the COVID-19 pandemic.</p>
    <p>Questions were manually extracted from official past papers published by BIEK and publicly available scanned papers. The dataset uses a <code>$</code> delimiter to separate MCQ answer choices and long-question sub-parts. All analysis below derives exclusively from this dataset.</p>
    <p>The three question types serve distinct assessment functions:</p>
    <ul style="margin-left: 20px; margin-bottom: 12px;">
      <li><span class="tag tag-mcq">MCQs</span> — Objective recall and recognition; typically 4 options per question</li>
      <li><span class="tag tag-short">Short</span> — Brief explanations, definitions, small programs, or conversion exercises</li>
      <li><span class="tag tag-long">Long</span> — Extended responses with multiple sub-parts covering conceptual depth and coding</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>Overall Question Type Distribution</h3>
    <div class="chart-row">
      <div class="chart-wrap"><canvas id="chartOverallPie"></canvas></div>
      <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: center;">
        <table class="data-table" style="max-width: 340px;">
          <thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Count</th><th>Share</th><th>Avg / Year</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><span class="tag tag-mcq">MCQs</span></td><td>150</td><td>45.9%</td><td>15.0</td></tr>
            <tr><td><span class="tag tag-short">Short</span></td><td>147</td><td>44.9%</td><td>14.7</td></tr>
            <tr><td><span class="tag tag-long">Long</span></td><td>30</td><td>9.2%</td><td>3.0</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================== SECTION 2 ============================== -->
<section class="section" id="yearly-distribution">
  <h2 class="section-title"><span class="section-number">2</span>Year-by-Year Question Volume Analysis</h2>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>Annual Question Counts by Type</h3>
    <div class="chart-wrap medium"><canvas id="chartYearlyStacked"></canvas></div>
    <table class="data-table" style="margin-top: 16px;">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Year</th><th>MCQs</th><th>Short</th><th>Long</th><th>Total</th><th>YoY Δ</th><th>YoY %</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>2015</td><td>15</td><td>9</td><td>3</td><td>27</td><td>—</td><td>—</td></tr>
        <tr><td>2016</td><td>15</td><td>9</td><td>3</td><td>27</td><td>0</td><td>0.0%</td></tr>
        <tr class="highlight"><td>2017</td><td>15</td><td>18</td><td>3</td><td>36</td><td>+9</td><td>+33.3%</td></tr>
        <tr><td>2018</td><td>15</td><td>18</td><td>3</td><td>36</td><td>0</td><td>0.0%</td></tr>
        <tr><td>2019</td><td>15</td><td>18</td><td>3</td><td>36</td><td>0</td><td>0.0%</td></tr>
        <tr class="missing"><td>2020</td><td colspan="6">No examination data (COVID-19 pandemic)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>2021</td><td>15</td><td>15</td><td>3</td><td>33</td><td>−3</td><td>−8.3%</td></tr>
        <tr><td>2022</td><td>15</td><td>15</td><td>3</td><td>33</td><td>0</td><td>0.0%</td></tr>
        <tr><td>2023</td><td>15</td><td>15</td><td>3</td><td>33</td><td>0</td><td>0.0%</td></tr>
        <tr><td>2024</td><td>15</td><td>15</td><td>3</td><td>33</td><td>0</td><td>0.0%</td></tr>
        <tr><td>2025</td><td>15</td><td>15</td><td>3</td><td>33</td><td>0</td><td>0.0%</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>Three Distinct Structural Eras</h3>
    <p>The data reveals three clear structural phases in exam design, each remarkably stable within itself:</p>
    <div style="margin: 16px 0;">
      <p><span class="era-badge era-1">Era 1: 2015–2016</span> <strong>27 questions per paper</strong> — 15 MCQs, 9 Short, 3 Long. The short-answer section was compact, with MCQs dominating the paper at 55.6% of questions.</p>
      <p><span class="era-badge era-2">Era 2: 2017–2019</span> <strong>36 questions per paper</strong> — 15 MCQs, 18 Short, 3 Long. A significant +33.3% jump in total questions, driven entirely by doubling the short-answer section from 9 to 18 questions. This was the peak volume era, with short questions claiming 50% of all items.</p>
      <p><span class="era-badge era-3">Era 3: 2021–2025</span> <strong>33 questions per paper</strong> — 15 MCQs, 15 Short, 3 Long. Post-pandemic, the exam settled at a middle ground — reducing short questions from 18 to 15 and achieving near-parity between MCQs and short questions (45.5% each).</p>
    </div>
    <div class="insight">
      <strong>Key finding:</strong> The MCQ count (15) and Long question count (3) have never changed across the entire 11-year span. All variation in exam volume is attributable solely to shifts in the Short question count, which has moved through three plateaus: 9 → 18 → 15.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>Total Questions Trend Line</h3>
    <div class="chart-wrap medium"><canvas id="chartYearlyLine"></canvas></div>
    <p style="font-size: .88rem; color: var(--c-muted);">The 2020 gap represents the absence of exam data during the COVID-19 pandemic. Year-over-year comparisons bridge 2019 to 2021.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================== SECTION 3 ============================== -->
<section class="section" id="question-type-analysis">
  <h2 class="section-title"><span class="section-number">3</span>Question Type Composition &amp; Trends</h2>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>Proportional Share of Question Types Over Time</h3>
    <div class="chart-wrap medium"><canvas id="chartTypeRatio"></canvas></div>
    <p>This stacked area chart shows how the <em>percentage</em> allocated to each question type shifted across eras:</p>
    <table class="data-table" style="margin-top: 12px; max-width: 600px;">
      <thead><tr><th>Era</th><th>MCQs %</th><th>Short %</th><th>Long %</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>2015–2016</td><td>55.6%</td><td>33.3%</td><td>11.1%</td></tr>
        <tr><td>2017–2019</td><td>41.7%</td><td>50.0%</td><td>8.3%</td></tr>
        <tr><td>2021–2025</td><td>45.5%</td><td>45.5%</td><td>9.1%</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <div class="insight">
      <strong>Structural shift:</strong> The exam has moved from being MCQ-dominant (55.6%) in early years to a balanced format where MCQs and Short questions share near-equal weight (45.5% each). Long questions have remained a constant minor component at 8–11%.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>Type-Specific Analysis</h3>
    <div class="chart-row">
      <div>
        <h3 style="color: var(--c-mcq);">MCQs — The Immovable Constant</h3>
        <p>Exactly <strong>15 MCQs per year</strong>, without exception, across all 10 active years. This suggests the MCQ section is structurally fixed within the exam blueprint, likely tied to a standardized Section A that carries a fixed mark allocation.</p>
        <p>MCQ topics cover a wide range of both C programming and database concepts, typically testing recall of definitions, syntax rules, and conceptual identification.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 style="color: var(--c-short);">Short Questions — The Variable Component</h3>
        <p>The short-answer section is the <strong>only flexible element</strong> in the exam structure. Its count has moved through three values: <strong>9</strong> (2015–2016), <strong>18</strong> (2017–2019), and <strong>15</strong> (2021–2025).</p>
        <p>This section encompasses definitions, small programs, code output prediction, mathematical-to-C expression conversion, and brief explanations — the broadest range of cognitive tasks.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div style="margin-top: 16px;">
      <h3 style="color: var(--c-long);">Long Questions — Deep but Unchanging</h3>
      <p>Exactly <strong>3 long questions per year</strong>, each typically containing 2–3 sub-parts (a, b, c). These questions consistently blend C programming and database topics — for instance, one sub-part may ask for a program while another asks to explain MS-Access objects. The structure is formulaic: usually one question on control structures/loops + program, one on operators/data types/file handling, and one on database models/DBMS/MS-Access.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>Short Questions: The Pivot Point</h3>
    <div class="chart-wrap medium"><canvas id="chartShortOnly"></canvas></div>
    <p>Zooming in on the short-answer count reveals the full story of exam structural changes. The 2017 expansion doubled the number of short questions, potentially reflecting a curriculum enrichment or a deliberate decision to test more topics at a shallower depth. The post-pandemic stabilization at 15 represents a compromise — more comprehensive than the original 9, but less burdensome than 18.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================== SECTION 4 ============================== -->
<section class="section" id="topic-patterns">
  <h2 class="section-title"><span class="section-number">4</span>Recurring Topics &amp; Question Content Patterns</h2>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>Most Frequently Tested Topic Areas</h3>
