<section class="section" id="exam-prep-insights">
  <h2 class="section-title"><span class="section-number">5</span>Strategic Insights for Exam Preparation</h2>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>Priority Framework for Students &amp; Teachers</h3>
    <p>Based on 10 years of data, examination topics can be organized into three tiers of preparation priority:</p>

    <div style="margin: 20px 0;">
      <h3 style="color: #e53e3e; font-size: 1rem; margin-bottom: 8px;">Tier 1 — Must Master (Appear Every Year, Multiple Questions)</h3>
      <ul class="checklist">
        <li><strong>Operators:</strong> Arithmetic, logical (&&, ||, !), relational (==, !=), assignment (=), unary (++, --), bitwise (&, |), ternary (?:). Tested as MCQs, short definitions, and within programs. Averaging 4.6 questions/year.</li>
        <li><strong>Functions:</strong> Function definition, prototypes, calling functions, return types, recursive functions, call by value vs. reference. Averaging 3.4 questions/year.</li>
        <li><strong>I/O &amp; Format Specifiers:</strong> printf(), scanf(), gets(), puts(), getc(), putchar(), and format codes (%d, %f, %c, %s, %lf). Averaging 4.4 questions/year.</li>
        <li><strong>Data Types:</strong> int, float, char, double — their sizes, ranges, and usage. Consistently tested at 3.6 questions/year.</li>
        <li><strong>MS-Access Objects:</strong> Table, Query, Form, Report, Macro, Module — purpose and usage. Averaging 4.4 questions/year.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div style="margin: 20px 0;">
      <h3 style="color: #d69e2e; font-size: 1rem; margin-bottom: 8px;">Tier 2 — High Priority (Appear Most Years, Reliable Exam Content)</h3>
      <ul class="checklist">
        <li><strong>Loops:</strong> for, while, do-while syntax; nested loops; loop output prediction exercises. ~2.8 questions/year.</li>
        <li><strong>Control Structures:</strong> if-else, else-if ladder, switch-case, break/continue statements. ~2.7 questions/year.</li>
        <li><strong>Database Keys:</strong> Primary, foreign, composite, candidate, super, alternate keys — definitions and usage. Growing to 3/year recently.</li>
        <li><strong>Database Models:</strong> Hierarchical, relational, network, object-oriented model descriptions. ~2.2 questions/year.</li>
        <li><strong>DBMS Fundamentals:</strong> DBA role, advantages of DBMS, RDBMS features, data dictionary concepts. ~2.3 questions/year.</li>
        <li><strong>DB Abbreviations:</strong> SQL, DML, DDL, DCL, TCL full forms and definitions. Tested regularly across years.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div style="margin: 20px 0;">
      <h3 style="color: #38a169; font-size: 1rem; margin-bottom: 8px;">Tier 3 — Emerging &amp; Supplementary (Growing Importance)</h3>
      <ul class="checklist">
        <li><strong>Normalization, ER Diagrams, ACID Properties:</strong> New additions in 2022–2025. Expect these to grow in future papers.</li>
        <li><strong>Structures, Unions, Pointers:</strong> Appearing in 2024–2025 papers. Signals a broadening of the C programming scope.</li>
        <li><strong>Arrays &amp; Strings:</strong> Present in post-2021 papers with increasing frequency.</li>
        <li><strong>File Handling:</strong> Data files, fopen/fclose, file modes. Sporadic but important for long questions.</li>
        <li><strong>Database Relationships:</strong> One-to-one, one-to-many, many-to-many — appear periodically in both short and long formats.</li>
      </ul>
